<title>USA: Troy, N.Y., $54 mln deal repriced, yields lowered.</title>
<headline>Troy, N.Y., $54 mln deal repriced, yields lowered.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Albany Corp said Wednesday it repriced $54.1 million Municipal Assistance Corp for the City of Troy, N.Y., lowering yields in several maturities and cutting the 2022 yield to 5.60 percent from 5.65 percent.</p>
<p>To see the preliminary pricing, double click on nN2039164.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>MUNICIPAL ASSISTANCE CORPORATION</p>
<p>RE: $54,144,664.25*</p>
<p>FOR THE CITY OF TROY</p>
<p>(A PUBLIC BENEFIT CORP. OF THE STATE OF NEW YORK)</p>
<p>GENERAL RESOLUTION BONDS</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>NOTE THE REPRICING ON THE 2011-2012, 2016 AND 2022 MATURITIES</p>
<p>ON THE CURRENT INTEREST PORTION.</p>
<p>ALSO, NOTE THE PRICE CHANGE ON THE 2000-2021 MATURITIES ON THE</p>
<p>CAB PORTION.</p>
